Experiment No.: 4
Title

Demonstration of If Statement in Arduino

Aim

To demonstrate the use of if-else conditional statements in Arduino.

Theory

The if statement is used to execute a block of code when a given condition is true. The else statement executes when the condition is false.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
USB Cable
Computer/Laptop
Procedure
Connect Arduino Uno to the computer.
Open Arduino IDE.
Write a program using an if-else condition.
Compile and upload the program.
Open Serial Monitor.
Observe the output.
Code
int value = 15;

void setup()
{
  Serial.begin(9600);

  if(value > 10)
  {
    Serial.println("Value is greater than 10");
  }
  else
  {
    Serial.println("Value is less than or equal to 10");
  }
}

void loop()
{
}
Output
Value is greater than 10
Result

The if-else statement was successfully demonstrated.

Conclusion

The working of conditional statements in Arduino programming was studied successfully.
